 "what": "Blind reconstruction of house fronts from archival HABS photographs, scored against the same survey's measured elevation drawings.",
 "source": "Historic American Buildings Survey (Library of Congress), public domain; scans from the Wikimedia Commons mirror -- the Library of Congress refused automated downloads on the day. Photographs and drawings were deleted after scoring; only these numbers are kept.",
 "method": [
  "Each photograph squared up from its own vanishing points (smc.facades.photo_rectify).",
  "The front panel cut out and given only its width and height in metres, read from the drawing's scale bar -- the priors the footprint and the lidar give in the city.",
  "The pipeline unchanged: segmentation, detector, extract_front.",
  "Openings marked on the drawing and matched to the predicted ones (centres within max(1.5 m, the opening's size), overlap IoU >= 0.1)."
 ],
 "protocol": "raw: the pipeline given only the panel's width and height (as the footprint and lidar give it); a predicted opening matches a drawn one when their centres are within max(1.5 m, the drawn opening's size) and they overlap (IoU >= 0.1), nearest first. aligned: the same after a per-axis scale and offset fitted on the matched centres (secondary: with three openings it absorbs most of the error).",
